        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "8a07ae8f-be8c-5621-8063-1548664935d2",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Del Mar Fairgrounds, Del Mar racetrack\n- Events: San Diego County Fair, Del Mar Fair\n- Organizations: Thoroughbred Club, Paramount Studios\n- People: Bing Crosby, Pat O'Brien\n- Topics: Bing Crosby's career\n\nFacts:\n- The Del Mar racetrack at the Del Mar Fairgrounds was built in 1937 by the Thoroughbred Club, whose founding members included Bing Crosby and Pat O'Brien, with Paramount Studios as the corporate sponsor.\n- Bing Crosby, born Harry Lillis Crosby Jr. on May 3, 1903, was an American singer and actor.\n- The Del Mar Fairgrounds is a 370-acre property that hosts the annual San Diego County Fair.\n- The annual San Diego County Fair was called the Del Mar Fair from 1984 to 2001.\n- Bing Crosby died on October 14, 1977.\n- Bing Crosby's warm bass-baritone voice helped make him the best-selling recording artist of the 20th century, with over one billion records, tapes, compact discs, and digital downloads sold worldwide.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "b19850fc-556c-5678-b459-a3da6be14798",
        "text": "Page: Del Mar Fairgrounds. Sentence: The Del Mar Fairgrounds is a 370 acre property that is the site of the annual San Diego County Fair (called the Del Mar Fair from 1984 to 2001).\nPage: Del Mar Fairgrounds. Sentence: Its Del Mar racetrack was built by the Thoroughbred Club in 1937 by founding members Bing Crosby and Pat O'Brien with Paramount Studios as corporate sponsor.\nPage: Bing Crosby. Sentence: Harry Lillis \"Bing\" Crosby Jr. ( ; May 3, 1903 – October 14, 1977) was an American singer and actor.\nPage: Bing Crosby. Sentence: Crosby's trademark warm bass-baritone voice made him the best-selling recording artist of the 20th century, having sold over one billion records, tapes, compact discs and digital downloads around the world.",
